Another idea: a sort of golem. A lot of strength and constitution and
a number of resistances. Poison resistance (no cardiovascular system),
sleep resistance (doesn't sleep), sickness resistance (not really
alive), immune to touch of death and similar attacks (not really
alive), unbreathing, and may be the only race immune to the effects of
an Amulet of Strangulation.

Doesn't eat food; corpses, food rations, K-Rations and the like are
useless (as with vampires). How it will get sustenance really depends
on what sort of golem we want.

One idea is that it feeds on metal, like a rust monster. This has the
advantage of almost limitless food, devouring weapons and tools and
armour and the like. You could even eat metallic rings. The
disadvantage is that you'd often have to eat something that would
normally be useful to you, and it would be hard to pick up intrinsics
because (as before) you can't eat corpses. Better hope you luck out on
the ring resistances. Also, you could rust - rust traps, bathing in
fountains and *especially* falling in water on Medusa's level could
lead to constitution abuse or even outright drain.

The other, much more challenging idea is that it's a sort of steam-
powered clockwork golem; it only can only subsist on water. Obviously,
this one wouldn't rust, but it would be far more difficult to stay
fed. You'd be quaffing from fountains and converting all your potions
into potions of water. Intrinsics would be almost impossible to pick
up except for polymorphing and being crowned. It would be like a
vampire all over again.

Starvation messages would have to be tweaked too...becoming hungry
would be reported as "need fuel", weakness would be "you switch to
emergency power" and fainting would be "you suffer a system failure".
At least there'd be no chance of choking from overeating.



